A||N||6||DaRkLoRD||Replica F1 gokart??||||14||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||11-22-2000||03:22 AM||||I had another crazy idea tonight.. why not build a gokart, powered by a 50hp air cooled engine, that was a replica of a full-sized formula 1 race car? Besides finding the money to pay for it (which is a problem in most projects.. hehe..) I don't see any reason why one couldn't be built for under $2,500... depending on the quality of the fiberglass body, how cheap an engine you could find, etc.. and it wouldn't use proper racing slicks either.. but it'd be fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>it'd need a fairly big track to race on though.. probably an actual road course.<P>comments?? or should I really try to stop coming up with ideas at 3am?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cheever2||11-22-2000||03:36 AM||||Engineers.  Always coming up with stuff.  <BR>Go for it.<BR>I love F-1's, but don't have a clue what to tell you.  I wouldn't be replying to you if I wasn't intrigued by the idea, though.  <P>Good luck.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||11-22-2000||08:29 AM||||send me your idea dimensions and i'll build you one in 3D Max.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> or you can save all your money and find a Formula Ford or Formula Mazda.. and have more HP for about $1000 more... ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-22-2000||09:45 AM||||There is an SCCA Formula 440/500 class. They use two stroke snowmobile (or similar) engines. Might be a bit more expensive, but it is very similar to what you were asking about.<BR>Go to this page... <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/wi/Hellifino/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/wi/Hellifino/</A> <BR>Check out the links at the bottom.<P>Raydar<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||11-23-2000||09:43 PM||||Hmm.. thanks for the link. how fast do snowmobile engines go?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000005||fropuff||11-23-2000||10:25 PM||||One of my friends at school has a kart with about a 400 in it from an older snowmobile.  It's kind of an all-terrain, and weighs about 5-600 pounds.  It's very big, but it can still go about 65-70.  Seems fast as crap.  I'm sure with a smaller body, and a newer engine, you could probably get around 100.  I saw one on eBay that said could go 140.  I think it's a bunch of crap, but it might be possible.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||11-23-2000||10:41 PM||||When I can drive and get a job, I want to build one from bottom up.  I will probably go for about a 200CC Honda engine.  I found one on eBay here that can go about 80.  It's got a Honda 125CC and a 6-speed!  That's cool.  That's what I was thinking of.  Cool idea.  It's at:  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=500459440" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=500459440</A> <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 11-23-2000).]||||reg||1
